        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nWhat is the value of [MATH: \\dfrac{4}{3} \\times (-5+3)^{-2} + \\dfrac{2}{3} ?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, we compute the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{4}{3} \\times ({\\color{red}-5} + {\\color{red}3})^{-2} + \\dfrac{2}{3} = \\dfrac{4}{3} \\times ({\\color{red}-2})^{-2} + \\dfrac{2}{3}]\n\nNext, notice that [MATH: (-2)^{-2}=\\dfrac{1}{(-2)^2} = \\dfrac{1}{4}.] So, we obtain:\n\n[MATH: (4)/(3) \u00d7 (\u2212 2)^{\u2212 2} + (2)/(3)|=; (4)/(3) \u00d7 (1)/(4) + (2)/(3)|=; (4 \u00d7 1)/(3 \u00d7 4) + (2)/(3)|=; (4 \u00d7 1)/(3 \u00d7 4) + (2)/(3)|=; (1)/(3) + (2)/(3)|=; 1]"
      },
