        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nFind the value of [MATH: 2 + \\left(-4\\right)^{-2} \\div \\left( 1.5 + \\dfrac{2}{15} \\right)^0.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nAny number raised to the power of [MATH: 0] equals [MATH: 1.] So, we have\n\n[MATH: \\left( 1.5 + \\dfrac{2}{15} \\right) ^0 = 1.]\n\nNext, we evaluate the negative exponent and get\n\n[MATH: \\left(-4\\right)^{-2} = \\dfrac{1}{(-4)^2} = \\dfrac{1}{16}.]\n\nSubstituting all these values into the expression, we obtain:\n\n[MATH: 2 + (\u2212 4)^{\u2212 2} \u00f7 (1.5 + (2)/(15))^{0}|=; 2 + (1)/(16) \u00f7 1|=; 2 + (1)/(16)|=; (32)/(16) + (1)/(16)|=; (33)/(16)]"
